# Gradle
#
# Every one of these is ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored
# `build/` matches a directory called `build` at ANY depth — including the Java
# package directory buildSrc/src/main/kotlin/com/heimdall/build/, whose sources
# were silently swallowed and never committed, leaving main unbuildable from a
# fresh clone while `git status` reported a clean tree. `out` and `bin` are just
# as plausible as package names, so they are anchored too.
#
# Add a deeper level here if a module is ever nested more than two directories
# down, rather than removing the anchors.
/.gradle/
/*/.gradle/
/build/
/*/build/
/*/*/build/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
/out/
/*/out/
/*/*/out/
/bin/
/*/bin/
/*/*/bin/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
